00:00:37.765 --> 00:00:40.780
- So Tony, one of the critics
actually that I once met said,

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:42.095
"Yeah, Tony's techniques,

00:00:42.095 --> 00:00:43.772
"they were great for
about a year and a half

00:00:43.772 --> 00:00:44.886
"and then they wore off."

00:00:44.886 --> 00:00:45.984
- [Tony] (laughs)

00:00:45.984 --> 00:00:46.983
- What do you say to that?

00:00:46.983 --> 00:00:48.248
- It is what it is.

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:49.093
It's real simple,

00:00:49.093 --> 00:00:50.369
if you don't work out you
don't get muscle, right?

00:00:50.369 --> 00:00:52.532
So I always tell people
there's a daily practice,

00:00:52.532 --> 00:00:53.722
like priming.

00:00:53.722 --> 00:00:55.049
If you don't do that,

00:00:55.049 --> 00:00:57.060
if you get up and you just
have no discipline whatsoever

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:58.253
you get no value of anything.

00:00:58.253 --> 00:00:59.664
Diets don't work when you don't do them,

00:00:59.664 --> 00:01:00.950
exercise doesn't work
when you don't do them.

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:03.061
But, most of the people
have some experiences

00:01:03.061 --> 00:01:04.358
that they want to shift,

00:01:04.358 --> 00:01:06.959
and once you shift those
things your whole life changes.

00:01:06.959 --> 00:01:08.476
But, life is constant growth.

00:01:08.476 --> 00:01:10.496
My life isn't here because I
went to one seminar one time

00:01:10.496 --> 00:01:12.314
and now my life is fit for life.

00:01:12.314 --> 00:01:13.377
I work out,

00:01:13.377 --> 00:01:14.557
I train my mind,

00:01:14.557 --> 00:01:15.390
I train my body,

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:16.731
it becomes a lifestyle.

00:01:16.731 --> 00:01:17.751
It's not just the,

00:01:17.751 --> 00:01:19.216
like you're depending upon somebody else.

00:01:19.216 --> 00:01:20.513
I'm not here to become somebody's guru,

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:21.896
I'm not here to give them a gift.

00:01:21.896 --> 00:01:23.280
I'm here to help them
open up their own gifts,

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:25.195
an that's really what my work has been.

00:01:25.195 --> 00:01:28.391
- I've never met a person
who was not successful

00:01:28.391 --> 00:01:31.554
that didn't have a great
amount of self-discipline

00:01:31.554 --> 00:01:33.235
within their life.

00:01:33.235 --> 00:01:36.332
Self-discipline and being able to perform

00:01:36.332 --> 00:01:39.225
and being able to keep
your life on schedule

00:01:39.225 --> 00:01:41.925
and being able to keep
commitments and promises

00:01:41.925 --> 00:01:45.508
and meet deadlines is
essential to success.

00:01:46.533 --> 00:01:47.842
None of us,

00:01:47.842 --> 00:01:51.033
none of us can afford to have
a life that is controlled

00:01:51.033 --> 00:01:53.853
by someone else or a
life that is basically

00:01:53.853 --> 00:01:55.870
controlled by our emotions.

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:59.679
I learned many years ago that
there are two kinds of people.

00:01:59.679 --> 00:02:01.560
There's the type of person who says,

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:04.834
"I'm going to wait until I
feel like it before I do it."

00:02:04.834 --> 00:02:06.311
And then there's the person who says,

00:02:06.311 --> 00:02:08.577
"I've got to do it so
that I feel like it."

00:02:08.577 --> 00:02:11.242
One will never get anything done

00:02:11.242 --> 00:02:14.165
because they're still waiting
to feel the moment to move

00:02:14.165 --> 00:02:15.610
and the other person that says,

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:16.920
"No, I need to move and then

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:19.879
"I will begin to feel the moment."

00:02:19.879 --> 00:02:23.451
Self-discipline is the
essential in your life

00:02:23.451 --> 00:02:26.898
and in my life if we're
going to get things done.

00:02:26.898 --> 00:02:29.973
So I have a challenge for
every one of you this weekend.

00:02:29.973 --> 00:02:31.322
The challenge is simple.

00:02:31.322 --> 00:02:33.323
As you go through your weekend

00:02:33.323 --> 00:02:34.883
and sometimes it's kind of a,

00:02:34.883 --> 00:02:37.840
hopefully an easier time of your week,

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:39.331
ask yourself,

00:02:39.331 --> 00:02:43.379
"Am I practicing
self-discipline in my life?

00:02:43.379 --> 00:02:45.174
"Am I doing the things that I should do

00:02:45.174 --> 00:02:47.961
"because I need to do them
or am I kind of waiting

00:02:47.961 --> 00:02:49.711
"to feel the moment?"

00:02:50.799 --> 00:02:52.913
Do like our friends Nike say.

00:02:52.913 --> 00:02:53.830
Just do it.

00:02:54.967 --> 00:02:56.805
- [Interviewer] How different
do you think your career

00:02:56.805 --> 00:02:58.376
and possibly your life would have been

00:02:58.376 --> 00:03:02.543
had you not embraced the
physical fitness part early on?

00:03:03.409 --> 00:03:04.242
- Oh man.

00:03:04.242 --> 00:03:05.707
You know, it just gives me,

00:03:05.707 --> 00:03:07.900
between my physical fitness and my faith

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:10.006
I have so much discipline in my life.

00:03:10.006 --> 00:03:13.919
And I have such a positive
outlook on life and you know,

00:03:13.919 --> 00:03:15.254
the opportunities that I have

00:03:15.254 --> 00:03:17.410
and the things that I've been
able to accomplish in my life.

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:18.946
So it starts out you know,

00:03:18.946 --> 00:03:20.479
I'm up at 4:30 in the morning,

00:03:20.479 --> 00:03:22.011
I'm in the kitchen having breakfast,

00:03:22.011 --> 00:03:23.351
5:00 I'm in the gym,

00:03:23.351 --> 00:03:25.468
6:30 I've already had another shake

00:03:25.468 --> 00:03:27.573
and 7:30 I'm eating a
couple turkey burgers,

00:03:27.573 --> 00:03:29.080
dropping the kids off at school

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:31.668
and by 9:00 I'm having another meal

00:03:31.668 --> 00:03:32.990
and I've already been
to church and worked out

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:34.172
and you know,

00:03:34.172 --> 00:03:35.005
I feel like there isn't anything
that I can't accomplish.

00:03:35.005 --> 00:03:37.338
- When I was in high school,

00:03:39.671 --> 00:03:43.004
I must've been maybe 16 or 17 years old.

00:03:44.278 --> 00:03:47.641
And I went rock climbing
in El Dorado Canyon,

00:03:47.641 --> 00:03:50.067
near where I grew up in Boulder.

00:03:50.067 --> 00:03:51.668
I'd been climbing about
three or four years

00:03:51.668 --> 00:03:54.058
and I went to do a climb called T2.

00:03:54.058 --> 00:03:54.891
Now at the time,

00:03:54.891 --> 00:03:56.888
T2 was a relatively difficult climb

00:03:56.888 --> 00:03:58.888
and I went at it with a,

00:04:00.685 --> 00:04:03.776
kind of an arrogant lack of preparation.

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:07.259
And I hadn't prepared for
being able to do certain kinds

00:04:07.259 --> 00:04:08.092
of finger cracks,

00:04:08.092 --> 00:04:10.348
I figured, "Oh, I'll figure
it out when I get there."

00:04:10.348 --> 00:04:12.065
And I also didn't pause,

00:04:12.065 --> 00:04:14.485
and this is the thing about
boldness and discipline,

00:04:14.485 --> 00:04:18.652
I didn't pause to really
double check all my systems.

00:04:20.203 --> 00:04:21.199
Okay.

00:04:21.199 --> 00:04:22.434
So I'm on the fourth pitch,

00:04:22.434 --> 00:04:26.241
I'm about 400 feet above the ground.

00:04:26.241 --> 00:04:29.967
I'm going across the slanting crack system

00:04:29.967 --> 00:04:33.381
that I'd started to have trouble with

00:04:33.381 --> 00:04:35.428
and my forearm started to engorge

00:04:35.428 --> 00:04:37.021
with blood and lactic acid.

00:04:37.021 --> 00:04:38.073
Which meas at some point,

00:04:38.073 --> 00:04:39.152
even if you're on a big hold,

00:04:39.152 --> 00:04:40.861
your hands are going to melt off.

00:04:40.861 --> 00:04:41.694
Okay.

00:04:41.694 --> 00:04:43.527
And I'm about to fall.

00:04:45.038 --> 00:04:46.616
I'm 400 feet above the ground.

00:04:46.616 --> 00:04:49.985
But it should be okay
because there's protection,

00:04:49.985 --> 00:04:51.519
I'm tied into the rope.

00:04:51.519 --> 00:04:54.398
I may take a fall but I'll get caught.

00:04:54.398 --> 00:04:55.269
For some reason,

00:04:55.269 --> 00:04:57.583
and to this day I still don't know why,

00:04:57.583 --> 00:05:01.666
my brain triggered that
I should look at my knot.

00:05:03.123 --> 00:05:05.753
And I looked down at my knot.

00:05:05.753 --> 00:05:07.753
My knot had come untied.

00:05:09.811 --> 00:05:13.047
I had made the mistake of
never really thinking about

00:05:13.047 --> 00:05:15.548
the best knot for certain
types of situations

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:17.304
and I tied in with what's a bowline.

00:05:17.304 --> 00:05:20.422
Now the advantage of a
bowline is it's easy to untie.

00:05:20.422 --> 00:05:21.718
Right?

00:05:21.718 --> 00:05:25.438
The disadvantage of a bowline
is it's easy to untie.

00:05:25.438 --> 00:05:29.163
It had come untied as
I kept moving across,

00:05:29.163 --> 00:05:32.246
and it is just hanging in my harness.

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:36.140
I'm seconds away from falling,

00:05:37.158 --> 00:05:39.428
only now I will die.

00:05:39.428 --> 00:05:42.067
I will die if I fall off.

00:05:42.067 --> 00:05:44.067
My forearms are melting.

00:05:45.457 --> 00:05:47.023
And the knot had come untied,

00:05:47.023 --> 00:05:48.842
and so I called down to my partner,

00:05:48.842 --> 00:05:49.964
I said, "My know came untied."

00:05:49.964 --> 00:05:50.934
What is he going to do?

00:05:50.934 --> 00:05:52.066
He can't do anything,

00:05:52.066 --> 00:05:53.729
he'll just watch me fall to my death.

00:05:53.729 --> 00:05:55.026
And I,

00:05:55.026 --> 00:05:57.350
there was an old fixed piton in the rock

00:05:57.350 --> 00:05:59.708
that was put there from the first descent,

00:05:59.708 --> 00:06:00.805
an old soft iron piton.

00:06:00.805 --> 00:06:01.798
And I looked at it,

00:06:01.798 --> 00:06:02.947
and I probably had 15,

00:06:02.947 --> 00:06:04.628
20 seconds before my hands would unwrap,

00:06:04.628 --> 00:06:05.713
if that,

00:06:05.713 --> 00:06:06.769
maybe 10.

00:06:06.769 --> 00:06:09.722
I took a runner and I
clipped it into the piton

00:06:09.722 --> 00:06:12.409
and I clipped the piton into my,

00:06:12.409 --> 00:06:14.850
that runner into my harness

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:17.991
and just went, "Please hold."

00:06:17.991 --> 00:06:19.074
And I let go.

00:06:20.458 --> 00:06:21.458
And it held.

00:06:22.617 --> 00:06:24.069
I put in a backup,

00:06:24.069 --> 00:06:25.238
I grabbed the knot,

00:06:25.238 --> 00:06:26.159
retied it,

00:06:26.159 --> 00:06:27.133
went to the ledge,

00:06:27.133 --> 00:06:28.277
I didn't convulse.

00:06:28.277 --> 00:06:29.322
I was very calm at that moment.

00:06:29.322 --> 00:06:31.760
When I got to the ledge I
went into convulsive shaking.

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:33.012
I was sick to my stomach for days

00:06:33.012 --> 00:06:36.262
because of whatever happens chemically.

00:06:37.202 --> 00:06:40.452
What I learned from that is two things.

00:06:41.617 --> 00:06:44.662
The first is that when you're
in an unforgiving world

00:06:44.662 --> 00:06:46.493
and gravity is unforgiving,

00:06:46.493 --> 00:06:48.444
it doesn't care.

00:06:48.444 --> 00:06:51.516
It never takes a day off, ever.

00:06:51.516 --> 00:06:54.614
And if you make one
mistake it can kill you,

00:06:54.614 --> 00:06:55.758
if it's the wrong kind of mistake.

00:06:55.758 --> 00:06:57.369
And what I learned is that sense of yeah,

00:06:57.369 --> 00:06:58.402
I want to do adventurous things,

00:06:58.402 --> 00:06:59.354
I want to climb rocks,

00:06:59.354 --> 00:07:00.416
I want to be in Yosemite,

00:07:00.416 --> 00:07:03.578
I want to do things that
get my adrenaline going.

00:07:03.578 --> 00:07:06.256
But, I need the discipline to always do

00:07:06.256 --> 00:07:07.826
all the right preparation.

00:07:07.826 --> 00:07:09.481
To always think about the right knots,

00:07:09.481 --> 00:07:11.358
to always be cross-checking my system

00:07:11.358 --> 00:07:14.113
so that I can do those bold things

00:07:14.113 --> 00:07:16.575
and stay alive in an
unforgiving environment.

00:07:16.575 --> 00:07:18.351
And as you and I spoke
about earlier today,

00:07:18.351 --> 00:07:20.304
I think that's the recipe,

00:07:20.304 --> 00:07:23.065
I think we are all heading
into an unforgiving environment

00:07:23.065 --> 00:07:25.997
where we're going to have to
be both bold and disciplined.

00:07:25.997 --> 00:07:28.706
The second thing I learned.

00:07:28.706 --> 00:07:32.216
What if that piton had not been there?

00:07:32.216 --> 00:07:34.940
We might not be here together.

00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:39.107
It was just by chance that
that piton was right there.

00:07:41.986 --> 00:07:43.776
I want you to realize
when you rewind the tape

00:07:43.776 --> 00:07:46.157
of your own life is that there
are these crucial moments

00:07:46.157 --> 00:07:49.574
where if the luck had gone the other way,

00:07:51.872 --> 00:07:54.272
you might have gotten killed.

00:07:54.272 --> 00:07:56.220
And so what you have to do is to always be

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:59.114
putting those extra disciplines in place,

00:07:59.114 --> 00:08:01.447
because I was lucky to live.

00:08:03.045 --> 00:08:04.512
And what I took from that is

00:08:04.512 --> 00:08:08.429
I never want to have to
be lucky to live again.

00:08:09.885 --> 00:08:11.886
I want to live because of my discipline,

00:08:11.886 --> 00:08:14.178
not because of my luck.

00:08:14.178 --> 00:08:16.773
- Going on perhaps a decade
of running simultaneously

00:08:16.773 --> 00:08:18.146
two global companies,

00:08:18.146 --> 00:08:20.560
how do you get the stamina to keep going

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:21.953
and to stay fit,

00:08:21.953 --> 00:08:24.801
you know, personally and
mentally and physically?

00:08:24.801 --> 00:08:25.698
- Well you know,

00:08:25.698 --> 00:08:29.865
somebody said with a little
discipline you do little things.

00:08:31.241 --> 00:08:33.299
With a lot of discipline
you do a lot of things

00:08:33.299 --> 00:08:36.669
and with the discipline there's
nothing which you cannot do.

00:08:36.669 --> 00:08:38.558
It requires a lot of discipline.

00:08:38.558 --> 00:08:39.447
I mean,

00:08:39.447 --> 00:08:42.039
obviously because you're
going to move from one work

00:08:42.039 --> 00:08:42.886
to the other,

00:08:42.886 --> 00:08:43.783
from one culture to the other,

00:08:43.783 --> 00:08:45.079
from two completely different companies.

00:08:45.079 --> 00:08:46.375
You have jet lag,

00:08:46.375 --> 00:08:47.284
disorganization.

00:08:47.284 --> 00:08:50.235
People are expecting you when
you come down from a plane

00:08:50.235 --> 00:08:54.091
after 14 hours flight to be
fresh and ready for them.

00:08:54.091 --> 00:08:56.688
They're not expecting to
see you to come and say,

00:08:56.688 --> 00:08:57.854
"Oh my god, this jet lag."

00:08:57.854 --> 00:08:59.457
You cannot answer the question.

00:08:59.457 --> 00:09:02.304
They want you to be on
the go all the time.

00:09:02.304 --> 00:09:04.820
So, this requires a lot of discipline.

00:09:04.820 --> 00:09:06.255
You have to organize yourself.

00:09:06.255 --> 00:09:07.088
If you know you're going to do this job

00:09:07.088 --> 00:09:09.792
and you accept the job you
have to organize yourself

00:09:09.792 --> 00:09:11.429
in order to do it.

00:09:11.429 --> 00:09:12.500
It's tough,

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:13.795
but there is a solution.

00:09:13.795 --> 00:09:15.312
There is a solution for it.

00:09:15.312 --> 00:09:16.610
But, it requires a lot of choices,

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:17.748
personal choices.

00:09:17.748 --> 00:09:19.550
There are a lot of things you cannot do.

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:20.798
You know?

00:09:20.798 --> 00:09:21.990
There are a lot of things you can do,

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:23.681
but you're going to do them
within a certain order,

00:09:23.681 --> 00:09:27.181
but particularly with a lot of discipline.

00:09:28.477 --> 00:09:30.810
- In 2009 when the mix tape,

00:09:31.689 --> 00:09:35.554
and there was a period where
I think around that time

00:09:35.554 --> 00:09:36.670
you were kind of like,

00:09:36.670 --> 00:09:40.873
"Is this something that's
going to work for me or not?"

00:09:40.873 --> 00:09:42.737
What is it that got you through,

00:09:42.737 --> 00:09:45.070
how'd you work through that?

00:09:47.897 --> 00:09:50.835
- Yeah, it's tough to
say exactly what it was.

00:09:50.835 --> 00:09:51.984
It was hard work,

00:09:51.984 --> 00:09:53.377
it was discipline,

00:09:53.377 --> 00:09:55.859
it was knowing that if
this doesn't work out

00:09:55.859 --> 00:09:58.454
then I will have to get a nine to five.

00:09:58.454 --> 00:10:00.352
And I don't want to do that,

00:10:00.352 --> 00:10:02.935
I really don't want to do that.

00:10:03.913 --> 00:10:08.080
And it was working with
Ryan and putting everything

00:10:09.190 --> 00:10:10.409
into the music,

00:10:10.409 --> 00:10:11.707
and you know, for,

00:10:11.707 --> 00:10:13.622
I mean leading up to
that point I think that

00:10:13.622 --> 00:10:15.616
you have to look at my track record.

00:10:15.616 --> 00:10:17.686
I had always wanted to get sober,

00:10:17.686 --> 00:10:19.360
I could never get sober.

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:22.694
I couldn't make music while
I was under the influence

00:10:22.694 --> 00:10:24.245
of drugs or alcohol.

00:10:24.245 --> 00:10:25.308
Finally got sober in 2008,

00:10:25.308 --> 00:10:26.997
got out of rehab and was like,

00:10:26.997 --> 00:10:28.068
alright this is it.

00:10:28.068 --> 00:10:29.546
I've wasted years of my life

00:10:29.546 --> 00:10:33.546
and if this is going to
work it has to work now.

00:10:34.572 --> 00:10:36.636
There is no alternative.

00:10:36.636 --> 00:10:40.803
And I met somebody that had
the same dedication as me.

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:43.992
That put everything into the music,

00:10:43.992 --> 00:10:46.084
everything into the craft,

00:10:46.084 --> 00:10:47.425
and didn't go out,

00:10:47.425 --> 00:10:50.650
they didn't really have many friends.

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:53.414
(laughter)

00:10:53.414 --> 00:10:54.247
Just kidding,

00:10:54.247 --> 00:10:55.530
just kidding.

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:58.421
We only hang out with each other.

00:10:58.421 --> 00:11:00.459
No, its somebody that
wasn't going to you know,

00:11:00.459 --> 00:11:01.616
be like, you know,

00:11:01.616 --> 00:11:03.586
up until that point I was
making music with people

00:11:03.586 --> 00:11:06.598
that were constantly putting
their priorities into getting--

00:11:06.598 --> 00:11:07.703
- Cooler people.

00:11:07.703 --> 00:11:08.536
- Getting,

00:11:08.536 --> 00:11:09.465
no, not at all.

00:11:09.465 --> 00:11:12.252
Getting loaded or chasing
women or whatever,

00:11:12.252 --> 00:11:13.645
and that's what I did for a long time

00:11:13.645 --> 00:11:14.768
and it didn't,

00:11:14.768 --> 00:11:16.114
it led me to being broke and in rehab

00:11:16.114 --> 00:11:18.826
and moving back into my parents' house.

00:11:18.826 --> 00:11:19.676
Which is awesome,

00:11:19.676 --> 00:11:23.658
but I wanted a career
and Ryan was somebody

00:11:23.658 --> 00:11:27.871
that had the same discipline
and sacrificed everything.

00:11:27.871 --> 00:11:29.919
- What my dad always told
us when we were growing up

00:11:29.919 --> 00:11:32.002
that if you end a dollar,

00:11:34.194 --> 00:11:35.813
you don't save anything.

00:11:35.813 --> 00:11:39.540
If you end it beyond the
light you won't save anything.

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:42.707
And so, that discipline of investment,

00:11:45.235 --> 00:11:46.068
keeping something,

00:11:46.068 --> 00:11:48.489
don't consume everything you get,

00:11:48.489 --> 00:11:51.043
actually helped me significantly.

00:11:51.043 --> 00:11:52.462
- Those star moments that you know,

00:11:52.462 --> 00:11:55.109
fill the highlight reels and you know,

00:11:55.109 --> 00:11:57.329
leave an audience in awe to watch,

00:11:57.329 --> 00:11:59.567
"Oh wow, play that again,
I want to see that."

00:11:59.567 --> 00:12:02.411
Those seconds are built
on thousands and thousands

00:12:02.411 --> 00:12:07.038
and thousands of hours that a
lot of people wouldn't think

00:12:07.038 --> 00:12:10.121
are worth adding to a highlight reel.

00:12:13.569 --> 00:12:17.722
Basic fundamentals being
applied over and over

00:12:17.722 --> 00:12:18.972
and over again.

00:12:20.655 --> 00:12:21.902
Getting up a certain time,

00:12:21.902 --> 00:12:23.495
doing certain things,

00:12:23.495 --> 00:12:25.262
cooking your meals,

00:12:25.262 --> 00:12:27.577
going to you know,

00:12:27.577 --> 00:12:28.676
do your cardio,

00:12:28.676 --> 00:12:30.627
walking through the disciplines,

00:12:30.627 --> 00:12:32.460
keeping the checklist,

00:12:33.717 --> 00:12:35.285
and staying on top of them.

00:12:35.285 --> 00:12:37.323
Those are the things that you know,

00:12:37.323 --> 00:12:40.290
when you string them
together start to create

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:42.588
your day of efficient action.

00:12:42.588 --> 00:12:44.393
The more likely you are
to string those days

00:12:44.393 --> 00:12:45.749
of efficient action together,

00:12:45.749 --> 00:12:47.342
the more likely it will be

00:12:47.342 --> 00:12:49.661
that you can set up your own success.

00:12:49.661 --> 00:12:50.992
- How would you personally describe

00:12:50.992 --> 00:12:53.075
your style of leadership?

00:12:55.320 --> 00:12:57.570
- Close to the human being.

00:12:58.456 --> 00:13:00.495
I think discipline is very important,

00:13:00.495 --> 00:13:01.670
very important,

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:03.837
but discipline's relative.

00:13:04.909 --> 00:13:09.646
Especially when I work
together with young players.

00:13:09.646 --> 00:13:11.979
Yeah, never lose the target.

00:13:15.675 --> 00:13:17.004
I don't know how to say it,

00:13:17.004 --> 00:13:17.837
never lose the target.

00:13:17.837 --> 00:13:18.876
Always stay focused on it,

00:13:18.876 --> 00:13:23.043
and so that's pretty good
because that's always, yeah.

00:13:25.877 --> 00:13:27.523
Think it's still possible.

00:13:27.523 --> 00:13:29.586
So there's not a right word in English--

00:13:29.586 --> 00:13:30.419
- Belief.

00:13:30.419 --> 00:13:32.582
- Yeah, for sure belief.

00:13:32.582 --> 00:13:34.103
It's a bit different to believe,

00:13:34.103 --> 00:13:35.398
believe is,

00:13:35.398 --> 00:13:38.587
you can believe in something
but you can lose belief

00:13:38.587 --> 00:13:39.858
quite easily,

00:13:39.858 --> 00:13:41.415
so to be stronger in that moment,

00:13:41.415 --> 00:13:42.920
things like this.

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:45.340
- I always wanted to win the World Cup,

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:47.103
and that was the reason I started.

00:13:47.103 --> 00:13:49.148
6And as the time went by,

00:13:49.148 --> 00:13:51.892
I started enjoying cricket

00:13:51.892 --> 00:13:54.966
and I started realizing
the challenges of cricket

00:13:54.966 --> 00:13:58.299
and my coach was instrumental,

00:13:58.299 --> 00:14:00.275
along with my brother.

00:14:00.275 --> 00:14:02.872
My elder brother, Rajit,

00:14:02.872 --> 00:14:05.622
to make me realize the importance

00:14:07.896 --> 00:14:10.396
of leading a disciplined life,

00:14:11.492 --> 00:14:13.186
a focused life,

00:14:13.186 --> 00:14:15.436
and to make me push harder.

00:14:19.789 --> 00:14:21.227
They found reasons,

00:14:21.227 --> 00:14:24.310
and even towards the end of my career

00:14:25.442 --> 00:14:28.054
I followed that formula.

00:14:28.054 --> 00:14:30.048
If I scored runs,

00:14:30.048 --> 00:14:32.669
let the rest of the world talk about it,

00:14:32.669 --> 00:14:34.618
I think about the next game.

00:14:34.618 --> 00:14:35.471
And that,

00:14:35.471 --> 00:14:36.908
right from my school days,

00:14:36.908 --> 00:14:40.000
became an unwritten formula,

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:41.620
an unwritten law at home,

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:43.414
that we don't talk about the last game,

00:14:43.414 --> 00:14:45.414
we talk about next game.

00:14:46.330 --> 00:14:48.844
And however many runs I scored,

00:14:48.844 --> 00:14:52.304
I wanted to go out and
score more than that.

00:14:52.304 --> 00:14:54.427
So, if I didn't score,

00:14:54.427 --> 00:14:56.813
I would have a restless night.

00:14:56.813 --> 00:14:58.511
If I scored runs,

00:14:58.511 --> 00:15:00.059
I would till have a restless night

00:15:00.059 --> 00:15:02.518
thinking that how am
I going to score more?

00:15:02.518 --> 00:15:03.790
And that's how it all happened,

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:06.820
I mean I normally don't discuss numbers,

00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:09.876
but this is something that I
must share with all of you.

00:15:09.876 --> 00:15:13.543
Towards the end of my
school cricket career,

00:15:15.784 --> 00:15:18.772
I'd already started playing
first class cricket.

00:15:18.772 --> 00:15:21.719
And the last season I can probably say

00:15:21.719 --> 00:15:25.555
that I averaged 1,025
because I only got out

00:15:25.555 --> 00:15:28.193
once in the whole season.

00:15:28.193 --> 00:15:29.813
(laughter)

00:15:29.813 --> 00:15:32.063
(applause)

00:15:34.833 --> 00:15:37.693
My brother and my coach
was instrumental in that

00:15:37.693 --> 00:15:40.443
because every time I scored runs,

00:15:41.705 --> 00:15:44.276
none of them said "well played" to me,

00:15:44.276 --> 00:15:48.558
and that's why in my farewell
speech I said to my coach,

00:15:48.558 --> 00:15:52.095
"At least now you can take a
chance by saying well done."

00:15:52.095 --> 00:15:55.705
There are no more matches in my career.

00:15:55.705 --> 00:15:59.017
But, something that I lived for

00:15:59.017 --> 00:16:02.901
was appreciation for my
coach and my brother,

00:16:02.901 --> 00:16:04.152
which never happened,

00:16:04.152 --> 00:16:07.011
and that was something which you know,

00:16:07.011 --> 00:16:10.011
kept me giving my best all the time.

00:16:11.893 --> 00:16:12.965
- Thank you guys so much for watching,

00:16:12.965 --> 00:16:15.012
I'd love to know what did
you think of this video,

00:16:15.012 --> 00:16:16.153
what was your favorite clip,

00:16:16.153 --> 00:16:17.699
and what are you going
to immediately apply

00:16:17.699 --> 00:16:19.564
to your life or to your business somehow.

00:16:19.564 --> 00:16:21.428
Also, how have you developed discipline

00:16:21.428 --> 00:16:23.024
and do you have any wisdom to share

00:16:23.024 --> 00:16:24.372
that others can learn from?

00:16:24.372 --> 00:16:25.495
Leave it down in the comments below,

00:16:25.495 --> 00:16:27.238
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:16:27.238 --> 00:16:29.406
Finally, I want to give a
quick shout out to Jude Gbekou,

00:16:29.406 --> 00:16:30.720
I hope I pronounced that okay.

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:31.940
Thank you so much, Jude,

00:16:31.940 --> 00:16:33.854
for picking up a copy of
my book "Your One Word",

00:16:33.854 --> 00:16:36.033
it really, really,
really means a lot to me

00:16:36.033 --> 00:16:37.747
and I hope you're enjoying it.

00:16:37.747 --> 00:16:38.819
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:16:38.819 --> 00:16:39.992
I believe in you,

00:16:39.992 --> 00:16:41.806
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:16:41.806 --> 00:16:43.739
and whatever your one word is,

00:16:43.739 --> 00:16:44.938
much love.

00:16:44.938 --> 00:16:46.438
I'll see you soon.

